Chapter 12
Business ethics, and the shapes fraud takes
أخلاقيات الأعمال وأشكال الاحتيال
The second half of this book changes subject. Chapters 1 to 11 were about things that might happen to a company. The remaining chapters are about what the people inside it do — which is a risk in exactly the sense Chapter 1 defined, and the only one where the management accountant is not merely an adviser but a participant with obligations of their own.
This chapter lays the foundation. It defines business ethics, works through the four concepts the syllabus names — fairness, integrity, due diligence and fiduciary responsibility — and then catalogues the forms business fraud takes, which is both an ethics topic and a control topic, because every fraud in the list is also a failure of something in Chapter 7.
Figure F812-01 is your map.
Figure F812-01. Chapter 12 roadmap: what ethics is, the four concepts, and the shapes fraud takes.
